'''Combat Level''' (commonly abbreviated as '''CB''') is a composite numeric rating that reflects a player's or non-player character's (NPC) overall martial power in EvilQuest. It is displayed above characters in the game world, on right-click target menus, and determines target threat color indicators as well as PvP wilderness combat brackets.

A player's combat level ranges from a minimum of '''Level 3''' up to a maximum of '''Level 172'''.

== Combat Level Formula ==
In EvilQuest, combat level is calculated deterministically from seven combat-related [[Skills|skills]]:
* [[Defence]]
* [[Hitpoints]]
* [[Weaponry]]
* [[Strength]]
* [[Ranging]]
* [[Light Magic]]
* [[Dark Magic]]

The calculation consists of two primary components: a '''Base Level''' (defensive prowess) and a '''Style Factor''' (the highest offensive combat discipline among Melee, Ranged, and Magic).

=== Mathematical Formula ===
The client game engine computes player combat level using the exact function:

:<math>\text{Base} = 0.25 \times (\text{Defence} + \text{Hitpoints})</math>

:<math>\text{Melee} = 0.325 \times (\text{Weaponry} + \text{Strength})</math>

:<math>\text{Ranged} = 0.325 \times \left(\left\lfloor \frac{\text{Ranging}}{2} \right\rfloor + \text{Ranging}\right)</math>

:<math>\text{Magic} = 0.325 \times \left(\left\lfloor \frac{\max(\text{LightMagic}, \text{DarkMagic})}{2} \right\rfloor + \max(\text{LightMagic}, \text{DarkMagic})\right)</math>

:<math>\text{Combat Level} = \left\lfloor \text{Base} + \max(\text{Melee}, \text{Ranged}, \text{Magic}) \right\rfloor</math>

=== Formula Breakdown ===
* '''Base Level''': Defence and Hitpoints contribute equally to every player's survivability. Each level of Defence or Hitpoints contributes exactly '''0.25''' (<math>1/4</math>) toward the combat level.
* '''Offensive Style Maxima''': A player is only evaluated by their single highest offensive combat style (<math>\max(\text{Melee}, \text{Ranged}, \text{Magic})</math>). Training secondary or tertiary styles does ''not'' increase your combat level until that style exceeds your current primary style.
* '''Melee Contribution''': Weaponry and Strength together contribute '''0.325''' per combined level (<math>0.325 \times (\text{Weaponry} + \text{Strength})</math>). At equal Weaponry and Strength, each melee level adds '''0.325''' combat factor.
* '''Ranged Contribution''': Ranging uses the formula <math>0.325 \times (\lfloor \text{Ranging}/2 \rfloor + \text{Ranging})</math>. For even Ranging levels, this simplifies to <math>0.325 \times 1.5 \times \text{Ranging} = 0.4875 \times \text{Ranging}</math>.
* '''Magic Contribution''': Magic takes the higher of either [[Light Magic]] or [[Dark Magic]] (<math>\max(\text{LightMagic}, \text{DarkMagic})</math>). It scales identically to Ranging at <math>0.325 \times (\lfloor \text{Magic}/2 \rfloor + \text{Magic})</math>.
* '''Flooring''': The sum of the Base and the dominant offensive style is rounded down to the nearest integer with <math>\lfloor \dots \rfloor</math>.

== NPC Combat Level Formula ==
Monsters and hostile NPCs calculate their combat level using a streamlined formula:

:<math>\text{NPC Combat Level} = \max\left(1, \left\lfloor 0.25 \times (\text{Defence} + \text{Health}) + 0.325 \times (\text{Attack} + \text{Strength}) \right\rfloor\right)</math>

NPC combat levels are always at least '''Level 1'''.

== Combat Level Extremes ==

=== Minimum Combat Level (Level 3) ===
A newly created character has the minimum starting combat stats:
* Defence: 1
* Hitpoints: 10
* Weaponry: 1
* Strength: 1
* Ranging: 1
* Light Magic: 0, Dark Magic: 0

:<math>\text{Base} = 0.25 \times (1 + 10) = 0.25 \times 11 = 2.75</math>
:<math>\text{Melee} = 0.325 \times (1 + 1) = 0.65</math>
:<math>\text{Ranged} = 0.325 \times (0 + 1) = 0.325</math>
:<math>\text{Magic} = 0.325 \times (0 + 0) = 0.0</math>
:<math>\text{Combat Level} = \lfloor 2.75 + \max(0.65, 0.325, 0.0) \rfloor = \lfloor 2.75 + 0.65 \rfloor = \lfloor 3.40 \rfloor = '''3'''</math>

=== Maximum Combat Level (Level 172) ===
A character with all combat skills maxed at the level cap of '''150''':
* Defence: 150
* Hitpoints: 150
* Weaponry: 150
* Strength: 150
* Ranging: 150
* Light Magic: 150, Dark Magic: 150

:<math>\text{Base} = 0.25 \times (150 + 150) = 0.25 \times 300 = 75.0</math>
:<math>\text{Melee} = 0.325 \times (150 + 150) = 0.325 \times 300 = 97.5</math>
:<math>\text{Ranged} = 0.325 \times (75 + 150) = 0.325 \times 225 = 73.125</math>
:<math>\text{Magic} = 0.325 \times (75 + 150) = 0.325 \times 225 = 73.125</math>
:<math>\text{Combat Level} = \lfloor 75.0 + \max(97.5, 73.125, 73.125) \rfloor = \lfloor 75.0 + 97.5 \rfloor = \lfloor 172.5 \rfloor = '''172'''</math>

== Build Archetypes & Specializations ==
The game engine categorizes combat profiles into specialized combat archetypes:
* '''Pure Builds''': A character that focuses almost exclusively on a single offensive combat style while keeping Defence minimal. In client logic, when a style represents at least '''90.2%''' of offensive combat weight (with style weight threshold &ge; 230), the character is classified as a Pure:
** ''Melee Pure'': Focuses on Weaponry and Strength.
** ''Ranged Pure'': Focuses on Ranging.
** ''Light Mage Pure'': Focuses on Light Magic.
** ''Dark Mage Pure'': Focuses on Dark Magic.
* '''Hybrid Builds''': Characters who distribute combat progression across two or more disciplines (e.g., Melee-Ranged, Melee-Mage, or Ranged-Mage), offering tactical flexibility in PvP and dungeon encounters.

== Calculation Examples ==

=== Example 1: Mid-Level Melee Warrior ===
* Defence: 50, Hitpoints: 55
* Weaponry: 60, Strength: 65
* Ranging: 30, Light Magic: 10, Dark Magic: 0

'''Calculations''':
# <math>\text{Base} = 0.25 \times (50 + 55) = 0.25 \times 105 = 26.25</math>
# <math>\text{Melee} = 0.325 \times (60 + 65) = 0.325 \times 125 = 40.625</math>
# <math>\text{Ranged} = 0.325 \times (15 + 30) = 0.325 \times 45 = 14.625</math>
# <math>\text{Magic} = 0.325 \times (5 + 10) = 0.325 \times 15 = 4.875</math>
# Dominant Style: <math>\max(40.625, 14.625, 4.875) = 40.625</math> (Melee)
# Combat Level: <math>\lfloor 26.25 + 40.625 \rfloor = \lfloor 66.875 \rfloor = '''66'''</math>

=== Example 2: Ranged Pure ===
* Defence: 1, Hitpoints: 70
* Weaponry: 1, Strength: 1
* Ranging: 80
* Magic: 0

'''Calculations''':
# <math>\text{Base} = 0.25 \times (1 + 70) = 0.25 \times 71 = 17.75</math>
# <math>\text{Melee} = 0.325 \times (1 + 1) = 0.65</math>
# <math>\text{Ranged} = 0.325 \times (40 + 80) = 0.325 \times 120 = 39.0</math>
# <math>\text{Magic} = 0.0</math>
# Dominant Style: <math>\max(0.65, 39.0, 0.0) = 39.0</math> (Ranged)
# Combat Level: <math>\lfloor 17.75 + 39.0 \rfloor = \lfloor 56.75 \rfloor = '''56'''</math>

